{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44246184",
      "title": "Submitting Data with Server Actions",
      "sourceHash": "74c9714ef0900e5bf36b128db7c03ddae3ef9ef49fb9f1cf2b7acbe70aba5ed7",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.16,
          "end": 5.19,
          "en": "So you can use React server components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.19,
          "end": 7.38,
          "en": "for executing server site code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.38,
          "end": 10.08,
          "en": "and for fetching data on the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.08,
          "end": 15.08,
          "en": "You can also use them for submitting data to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.87,
          "end": 20.16,
          "en": "And for that, attached, you find another new component file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 20.16,
          "end": 23.04,
          "en": "which you should add into your components folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.04,
          "end": 27.777,
          "en": "And that's the ServerActionsDemo.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 27.777,
          "end": 32.25,
          "en": "And this file includes another server component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 32.25,
          "end": 35.22,
          "en": "React component decorated with async.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 35.22,
          "end": 39.6,
          "en": "But this is now a component that also includes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 39.6,
          "end": 44.313,
          "en": "a function that is actually used as a form action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 45.48,
          "end": 49.56,
          "en": "So this saveUserAction function is passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 49.56,
          "end": 51.617,
          "en": "to the action prop as you learned it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 51.617,
          "end": 55.443,
          "en": "in the form actions section earlier in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 60.57,
          "en": "But there is something special about this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 60.57,
          "end": 65.57,
          "en": "And the special thing here is this use server directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 67.92,
          "end": 71.19,
          "en": "This is something that can be added to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 71.19,
          "end": 76.19,
          "en": "a form action function to turn it into a server action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 76.32,
          "end": 79.65,
          "en": "And it then must be a async function too,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 79.65,
          "end": 81.63,
          "en": "that's also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 81.63,
          "end": 84.75,
          "en": "But if you have an async form action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 84.75,
          "end": 89.07,
          "en": "and you then add this use server directive inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 89.07,
          "end": 92.16,
          "en": "you convert it to a server action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 92.16,
          "end": 96.42,
          "en": "And a server action is, in the end, a form action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 98.49000000000001,
          "en": "which is a default React feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 98.49000000000001,
          "end": 102.6,
          "en": "that can be used in all React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 102.6,
          "end": 105.47999999999999,
          "en": "But it's a form action that's actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 105.47999999999999,
          "end": 109.413,
          "en": "executed on the server side, not on the client side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 110.58,
          "end": 113.85,
          "en": "And it's created by adding this use server directive.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 113.85,
          "end": 117,
          "en": "But because of that, it's now a feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 117,
          "end": 120.543,
          "en": "that's not available in all React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 121.38,
          "end": 124.2,
          "en": "So whilst form actions can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 124.2,
          "end": 129.18,
          "en": "in any React project out there and require no special setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 129.18,
          "end": 132.42,
          "en": "server actions do require a special setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 132.42,
          "end": 134.553,
          "en": "a special project, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 135.42,
          "end": 139.23,
          "en": "Because this code inside of this function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 139.23,
          "end": 144.23,
          "en": "will now be executed on the server, not on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 147.93,
          "en": "If you add a console log statement here and maybe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 147.93,
          "end": 152.46,
          "en": "a log executed, you will not find this log",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 152.46,
          "end": 154.503,
          "en": "in the browser developer tools.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 155.43,
          "end": 159.99,
          "en": "So if you save this and you go to the page.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 159.99,
          "end": 164.99,
          "en": "and there you output this ServerActionsDemo component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 165.06,
          "end": 166.86,
          "en": "and if you save that file as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 166.86,
          "end": 171.86,
          "en": "then you'll see this component here on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 172.11,
          "end": 175.5,
          "en": "And if you then enter some data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 175.5,
          "end": 177.99,
          "en": "and you open your browser developer tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 177.99,
          "end": 181.2,
          "en": "and the console there and you click Save User,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 181.2,
          "end": 182.643,
          "en": "you won't see anything here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 186.42,
          "en": "But if you go to your backend terminal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 186.42,
          "end": 188.733,
          "en": "you'll see executed here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 189.69,
          "end": 192.06,
          "en": "And this proves that this code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 192.06,
          "end": 194.28,
          "en": "was executed on the server side.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 194.28,
          "end": 196.98,
          "en": "And that's the idea behind server actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 196.98,
          "end": 200.57999999999998,
          "en": "which is another feature that's part of React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 200.57999999999998,
          "end": 204.32999999999998,
          "en": "but that's only available in projects that support it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 204.32999999999998,
          "end": 206.823,
          "en": "like this Next.js project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 208.77,
          "end": 212.91,
          "en": "Now when it comes to working with server actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 212.91,
          "end": 217.17000000000002,
          "en": "there are a couple of important things to understand.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 217.17000000000002,
          "end": 222.09,
          "en": "For example, you can only define such a server action here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 222.09,
          "end": 226.233,
          "en": "inside of a component if it's not a client side component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 227.22,
          "end": 231.6,
          "en": "So if I had use client here at the top of this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 231.6,
          "end": 233.64,
          "en": "we would get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 233.64,
          "end": 236.88,
          "en": "We would get the error that it's not allowed to use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 236.88,
          "end": 240.243,
          "en": "this use server directive in a client component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 241.23,
          "end": 244.05,
          "en": "Which I guess makes sense because we're now essentially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 244.05,
          "end": 247.95,
          "en": "telling the bundler, the build process,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 247.95,
          "end": 252.42,
          "en": "that this file should contain code that runs on the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 252.42,
          "end": 254.91,
          "en": "but then we tell it that we have code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 254.91,
          "end": 258.54,
          "en": "that should run on the server, not on the client.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 258.54,
          "end": 261.618,
          "en": "And this is kind of contradicting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 261.618,
          "end": 265.756,
          "en": "So that's why you can't have both in the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 265.756,
          "end": 270.756,
          "en": "However, you can use server actions in client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 270.96,
          "end": 273.213,
          "en": "You just can't define them there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 278.76,
          "en": "What you could do is grab that server action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 278.76,
          "end": 283.11,
          "en": "and then add a new actions folder, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 283.11,
          "end": 284.823,
          "en": "though the name doesn't matter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.23,
          "en": "and then add a file with any name of your choice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 289.23,
          "end": 292.593,
          "en": "and put your server action in there and export it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 297.87,
          "en": "And, that's all important, remove the use server directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 297.87,
          "end": 302.25,
          "en": "from the function and instead added at the top of this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 302.25,
          "end": 306.57,
          "en": "This is allowed by React in projects that support",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 306.57,
          "end": 311.49,
          "en": "this feature and this simply tells React and next JS here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 311.49,
          "end": 316.41,
          "en": "that this file only contains server actions in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 316.41,
          "end": 319.98,
          "en": "That's what putting use server at the top does.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 322.41,
          "en": "So this is now also a server action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 322.41,
          "end": 326.01,
          "en": "and you can indeed now go to your component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 326.01,
          "end": 329.64,
          "en": "and remove this import here and actually put that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 329.64,
          "end": 332.64300000000003,
          "en": "into the actions file, because it's needed there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 334.40999999999997,
          "end": 337.83,
          "en": "And then here in the server actions demo file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 337.83,
          "end": 341.307,
          "en": "you can simply import this saveUserAction",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 343.47,
          "end": 347.04,
          "en": "from this actions folder and the user's file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 347.04,
          "end": 350.973,
          "en": "And then still use that as a value for the action prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 351.96,
          "end": 355.17,
          "en": "So importing it and using it is allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 355.17,
          "end": 357.12,
          "en": "Defining it in the same file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 357.12,
          "end": 360.45,
          "en": "if it's a client component file, is not allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 360.45,
          "end": 363.33,
          "en": "Because when you import that server action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 363.33,
          "end": 366.51,
          "en": "this underlying build process is again able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 366.51,
          "end": 369.18,
          "en": "to split the code accordingly",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 369.18,
          "end": 371.94,
          "en": "and put this code on the client side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 371.94,
          "end": 375.78,
          "en": "but put the imported code on the server side, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 375.78,
          "end": 377.22,
          "en": "But it's not able to do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 377.22,
          "end": 379.173,
          "en": "if you have both in the same file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 380.31,
          "end": 383.67,
          "en": "Of course now since I added use client here, you also have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 383.67,
          "end": 387.09,
          "en": "to remove the async keyword here on this component though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 387.09,
          "end": 390.093,
          "en": "since client components can't be asynchronous.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 391.71,
          "end": 394.29,
          "en": "But with that done, if you reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 394.29,
          "end": 396.69,
          "en": "any errors here should be gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 396.69,
          "end": 401.13,
          "en": "And you can again submit that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 401.13,
          "end": 404.64,
          "en": "That again works and all that data is being saved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 404.64,
          "end": 408.12,
          "en": "if you take a look at this dummy-db.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 408.12,
          "end": 410.703,
          "en": "The data was stored there indeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 412.11,
          "end": 415.38,
          "en": "So that's what you should know about server actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 415.38,
          "end": 419.31,
          "en": "Another feature built into React that doesn't work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 419.31,
          "end": 421.89,
          "en": "in all React projects, but it does work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 421.89,
          "end": 424.563,
          "en": "in Next.js projects, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}